      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jphacks/tkb_2615/git/trees/638577dee470eadec3d92471378034087353ada9"
    },
    "message": "Hold the EventQueue in Rust, write each EventLog record's bytes on appending, and let a save read the live log\n\nRust owns the pending events (state/events.rs) and, as before, the realized log. A record appended\nfrom Python gets its canonical bytes in the same step; a rule's EventRow needs no Python object, and\none is built when Python reads it. A log that wrote all its bytes is its own restored log, so a\nsave's restore check no longer parses them or compares them with the objects. The information step\nis the first rule to schedule through EventWriter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
